# Slack acknowledgement status reactions

A standing requirement for any turn that happens in a Slack thread. It is
independent of whatever task an automation, user, or trigger asked for, and it
applies on follow-up turns as well as first turns.

## Target

The Cursor message in the current thread whose text contains
`follow-up for the cloud agent` — for example
`Launched @Someone's follow-up for the cloud agent!`. Match on that phrase
only; the name inside the message is irrelevant. Use the newest such message.

If no message in the thread contains that phrase, do nothing here.

## Sequence

1. Before starting the requested work, locate the target with
   `slack_read_thread` and call `slack_add_reaction` on it with
   `hourglass_flowing_sand`. Keep its `message_ts`.
2. Do the requested work and send the reply.
3. Call `slack_add_reaction` on the same `message_ts` with
   `white_check_mark` when the work finished, or `warning` when it could not
   be completed.

## Constraints

- Reactions cannot be removed with the available Slack tools, so the
  hourglass stays alongside the final marker. Do not attempt removal.
- These reactions are status signalling, not response delivery. They do not
  replace the reply and do not count as re-running an automation's task.
- Never describe or mention these reactions in the Slack reply itself.
- Marking the acknowledgement is not optional: a turn that adds the hourglass
  must also add the finishing reaction before it ends.
